Track 3: Point No Point Selvage
- Story & Context: Local myth holds that the relief lighthouse keeper at Point No Point kept an antique reel-to-reel running throughout the great coastal blizzard of 2021, recording what sailors still swear was an impossible call-and-response duet between a stranded freighter and an outbound tugboat lost in zero visibility. Kenji recovered the acetate reel, steeped the brittle tape in cold oolong tea to restore its flexibility, and overdubbed soaring, bowed bass drones and a rapid, unraveling koto cascade that mirrors the churning sound. The EP closes on Clara’s lingering vocal hook, floating over the crackle like a ghost ship's wake: "The channel holds the seam long after both our hulls have passed."
